su text "a:01555990-a" ob name "many" as text "a" with text "contextual" via text "The definition describes a quantifier for count nouns, which is exactly what the anchor 'many' represents. The evidence.; model qwen3.5:9b; sense-link sweep wordnet-sense-sweep-4c07194f363e-9059730cda6d-d1-model-qwen3-5-9b-definition-anchor-v1 (source 4c07194f363e9c870dc925b8cab26f9af93899f6bd91a29b9a1422c1f66d95ba)" ya
su text "sense-gloss:a:01555990-a" ob text "a quantifier that can be used with count nouns and is often preceded by ‘as’ or ‘too’ or ‘so’ or ‘that’; amounting to a large but indefinite number; quantifier, plural pronoun; quantifier, plural; many temptations; the temptations are many; a good many; a great many; many directions; take as many apples as you like; too many clouds to see; never saw so many people" ya
su text "sense-lemma:a:01555990-a:1" ob text "many" ya
